     "result_text_tail": "s no sales-lift data.\n- The nine weak stores' losses and sales are split evenly, which is what gives the 6/3 split between lapsing and long leases.\n- 65% of shrink responds to staffing (fresh waste plus receiving errors).\n- Sales and other cost trends are held at FY2025 levels. Private label is the exception: it keeps its current growth pace.\n- Promotions and fees start in the second quarter of FY2026.\n\n**A timing problem in the pack:** fiscal years end in January, so FY2026 should already be closed by a February 2027 board meeting. I followed the pack and treated FY2026 as the first plan year and the covenant year. Please check the dates before the meeting.\n\n**Decisions I made in your place:**\n- Navy theme.\n- Audience: the board, with the CEO presenting.\n- Storyline approved without your review.\n- I kept the 3.0% target and showed what closes the gap, rather than lowering the target.\n\nAll 165 numbers are taken from the briefing pack with verbatim excerpts or calculated from them with live formulas, and no placeholders remain. The builder script is in `./work/build_spec.py` if you want to change an assumption and re-run.\n\nI can switch the theme or re-run with different assumptions; the promotions volume-loss share is the one that matters most.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- harlow-margin-plan.pptx (22 slides: 15 content, 4 section dividers, cover, executive summary, next steps)\n- harlow-margin-plan-sources.xlsx\n- harlow-margin-plan.json (the spec the deck is rendered from)"
